--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- shallow-water chain under a steep Dean stream-function wave, 60 s
-- The grounded R4 chain of chain_catenary_shallow_30m.dat (30 m depth, fairlead held at the
-- surface) under a regular nonlinear stream-function wave, H = 8 m, T = 10 s (H/d = 0.27),
-- with 20 Fourier terms (StreamOrder) and a 10 s start-up ramp. The stream-function crest is
-- higher and sharper and its trough shallower and flatter than the linear wave of the same
-- height. Compare with airy_wave_shallow_chain.dat (same H and T, linear Airy theory).
